  <!--
    Why Costura: IfcComBridge.dll is an in-process COM server, so it runs in the host's process under the host's
    configuration. Its own .config file, and with it any binding redirect, is never read, yet its
    dependencies disagree on versions (Xbim.Common is built against Microsoft.Extensions.Logging 2.1.1,
    3.1.3 ships). Costura embeds the managed dependencies and resolves them by name at run time, so the
    library is self-contained and needs no binding redirects of its own. A host's own redirects can still
    interfere (docs/known-issues.md, KI-1). The native Xbim.Geometry.Engine64.dll cannot be loaded from
    inside the library: deploy it next to IfcComBridge.dll.
